Original code in this repository: MIT (see LICENSE).

OpenCode (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode): MIT. The server, its web interface and its CLI are built from upstream
sources by the GitHub Actions workflows and are part of every APK and every over-the-air update.

proot, libtalloc and the proot loader: the launcher that runs the Linux userland without root. They are taken from the
Termux package repository (https://packages.termux.dev) while the APK is built, renamed (libproot.so, libproot-loader.so,
libtalloc.so) and bundled unmodified apart from the library names. proot is GPL-2.0-or-later and libtalloc is LGPL-3.0-or-later.
Sources: https://github.com/proot-me/proot, https://github.com/termux/proot, https://github.com/termux/termux-packages and
https://www.samba.org/ftp/talloc/. A GPL notice must accompany a distributed APK; this file is that notice, and the
source locations above are where the corresponding source can be obtained.

Ubuntu 24.04 userland (https://ubuntu.com): the root filesystem archive inside the APK is made from the official Ubuntu
image and contains many packages under their own licenses (GPL, LGPL, MIT, BSD, Apache-2.0 and others). Their license
texts are inside the filesystem under /usr/share/doc/*/copyright, and sources are available from https://archive.ubuntu.com.

Added on top of Ubuntu while the archive is built: Node.js (MIT, https://nodejs.org), uv and uvx (MIT or Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/astral-sh/uv), ripgrep (MIT or Unlicense), git (GPL-2.0), Python (PSF-2.0).

wireproxy (https://github.com/pufferffish/wireproxy), bundled as libwireproxy.so: the Cloudflare WARP tunnel client.
It is downloaded from the official release while the APK is built and bundled unmodified apart from the name.
wireproxy is GPL-3.0; its license text is at the link above, and that is where the corresponding source can be
obtained.

sing-box (https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box), bundled as libsingbox.so: the local VLESS/Hysteria2 proxy engine for
user-imported VPN subscriptions. The pinned official linux-arm64 release (v1.12.9) is downloaded while the APK is
built and bundled unmodified apart from the name; its LICENSE file ships inside the APK as
assets/sing-box-LICENSE.txt. sing-box is GPL-3.0, and the link above is where the corresponding source can be
obtained.

Android platform libraries are used under their own terms and are not redistributed.

If you do not want to carry GPL obligations, keep your APK private: do not publish the releases of your fork.
